{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15426202","formula":"C₂₁H₂₄O₈","hill":"C21H24O8","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":24.0,"O":8.0},"names":{"en":"Mallotophenone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Mallotophenone is a dimeric phloroglucinol found in Mallotus oppositifolius or in Mallotus japonicus. The bioassay-guided fractionation of an ethanol extract of the leaves and inflorescence of M. oppositifolius collected in Madagascar led to the isolation of the two new bioactive dimeric phloroglucinols mallotophenone, together with mallotojaponins B and C. Diphenylmethanes are compounds that contain diphenylmethane moiety, which is a methane wherein two hydrogen atoms are replaced by two phenyl groups. Mallotophenone is strong as it has a very solid basic compound (based on its pKa).These compounds show antiproliferative and antiplasmodial activities."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":179090,"mass":404.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=C(C(=C(C(=C1OC)CC2=C(C(=C(C(=C2O)C(=O)C)O)C)OC)O)C(=O)C)O","inchikey":"JXSPGOIAWPYMGS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[3-[(3-acetyl-2,4-dihydroxy-6-methoxy-5-methylphenyl)methyl]-2,6-dihydroxy-4-methoxy-5-methylphenyl]ethanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"179090","atoms":53,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.208,"y":-2.514,"z":-1.411,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.211,"y":2.558,"z":-1.332,"el":"O"},{"x":1.278,"y":2.129,"z":-0.289,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.293,"y":-2.123,"z":-0.382,"el":"O"},{"x":4.655,"y":-0.797,"z":1.417,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.69,"y":0.74,"z":1.39,"el":"O"},{"x":3.266,"y":2.102,"z":2.432,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.498,"y":-2.526,"z":0.579,"el":"O"},{"x":0.001,"y":0.028,"z":-1.678,"el":"C"},{"x":1.232,"y":-0.19,"z":-0.858,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.256,"y":0.217,"z":-0.855,"el":"C"},{"x":1.789,"y":-1.465,"z":-0.76,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.798,"y":1.486,"z":-0.727,"el":"C"},{